# Title: Potential SentinelOne Shell Context Menu Scan Command Tampering
# ID: 6c304b02-06e6-402d-8be4-d5833cdf8198
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2024-03-06
# Tags: attack.persistence
# Description: Detects potentially suspicious changes to the SentinelOne context menu scan command by a process other than SentinelOne.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog ((registry_key_name="*\\shell\\SentinelOneScan\\command\\*") AND NOT ((((process_path="*C:\\Program Files\\SentinelOne\\" OR process_path="*C:\\Program Files (x86)\\SentinelOne\\")) OR ((Details="C:\\Program Files\\SentinelOne\\Sentinel Agent*" OR Details="C:\\Program Files (x86)\\SentinelOne\\Sentinel Agent*") AND Details="*\\SentinelScanFromContextMenu.exe*"))))
